  "provenance": "SupersonicLabs/Julia-1@a85b127321d580d65176c89ced8273f305745d85 (Apache-2.0; mmBERT-small with a decision head, 144M parameters) converted to classic LiteRT graphs in the host-lookup form: the graph takes the looked-up token embeddings (inputs_embeds), the token table ships as a flat float16 file (the checkpoint's float32 table rounded; measured effect on the probabilities at most 0.0077), and the tokenizer is the publisher's tokenizer.json (mmBERT / Gemma vocabulary, 256,000 tokens). One static window per graph (512 and 1024 tokens). The publisher's runtime applies no calibration (T=1) and has no act head. GPU FP32 only: on the verified phone the fp16 paths (GPU default precision, NPU) change answers, so no NPU profile is declared.",
